ing errors, as this can be seen as a form of \"admitting\" the limitations.\n3. **Feedback Mechanism**: The feedback mechanism might not always lead to an acknowledgment of the model's shortcomings or lack of knowledge.\n\nIn summary, while it is theoretically possible for LLMs to admit their limitations, practical implementation and algorithmic design can sometimes prevent this from happening.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nAnecdotally I've never had an LLM admit to me that it cannot answer my question. Instead , they will answer something wrong, which they will admit after I point it out to them, but then continue to give wrong answers to the same question regardless<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n","generated":""}
